li: FYI opened a docs PR that standardizes the streaming + pagination snippets across py/ts/go and adds a small 'checkpoint' utility to retain the last seen page cursor across transient retries. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/499

kevin: nice, can you paste the Go example here? i want to sanity-check the error handling pattern.

li: sure, here's the concise Go snippet i added to the snippet file (also added async/sync py + ts):

li: ```go
// go snippet (stream pages with checkpointed resume)
ctx := context.Background()
client := redwood.NewClient()
checkpoint := ""
for {
  pages, err := client.StreamPages(ctx, &redwood.StreamOptions{PageToken: checkpoint})
  if err != nil {
    // transient retry with backoff (helper below)
    if !isTransient(err) {
      log.Fatalf("stream failed: %v", err)
    }
    time.Sleep(backoffWithJitter())
    continue
  }
  for page := range pages {
    processPage(page)
    if page.NextToken != "" {
      checkpoint = page.NextToken
    }
  }
  // exit when no more pages
  if checkpoint == "" {
    break
  }
}
```

li: key point: we persist checkpoint between retry attempts so we avoid re-reading from page 1 if the stream dies mid-iteration.

kevin: looks good. one nit: prefer context with timeout on the top-level loop and use a small helper that centralizes backoff params. also please add a one-line note that consumers may opt to persist checkpoint to durable storage if they need cross-process resume.

li: added both notes and pulled the backoff helper into the docs-utils package. updated the TS snippet to show awaiting the call factory and the py examples to demonstrate both sync generator and async iterator variants.

sara: flagged two things in the PR review: (1) the legacy anchor /docs/streams#pagination still exists in other pages, we should update them to /docs/reference/streaming#pagination (2) docs/snippets/go/streaming.md had a gofmt diff in CI.

